mkvplex changelog
=================

0.13.0
------
- Refactored the ~400 KB single-file implementation into logical modules under particulars/.
- Added a thin root main.py entry point and package compatibility facade.
- Separated models/state, naming, media probing/splitting, disc inference, TMDb, filesystem operations, movie, collection, retail-volume, TV planning, TV orchestration, and CLI concerns.
- Preserved discovery schema 16; version change intentionally invalidates version-bound dry-run approvals, so generate a fresh dry run before execution.
- Added GitHub-facing README.md, compact README.txt, and packaged regression tests.

0.12.9
------
- Added authored MKV chapter-topology refinement for numbered retail-volume program alignment.
- Allowed decisive same-disc adjacent identity correction when multipart metadata and authored boundaries disagree.
- Pinky and the Brain Volume 2: resolves D3 as Brain Noir and D4 as Larry / Mousealopes from source evidence.

0.12.8
------
- Added chronological air-date ordering as a retail-volume metadata fallback.

0.12.7
------
- Added partial-volume support for usable TMDb DVD episode-group ordering while keeping complete-series ordering strict.

0.12.6
------
- Added play-all master content-order discovery using encoded video packet fingerprints and persistent DB caching.

0.12.5
------
- Corrected numbered retail-volume boundary placement using observed volume width.

0.12.4
------
- Added generic numbered retail-volume structural analysis, physical program-unit mapping, multi-segment splitting, and bonus/master archival.

0.12.3
------
- Treated numbered retail-volume labels as packaging metadata rather than series identity.
